sequenceDiagram
    participant U as 👤 User's Browser
    participant KAINAM as KAINAM App (App Runner)
    participant Auth as Auth Service (ALB -> Keycloak)

    U->>KAINAM: 1. Access https://<subdomain>.kainam.app
    KAINAM-->>U: 2. Return frontend app
    Note right of U: App detects no active session,<br/>initiates login.
    U->>Auth: 3. Redirect to Keycloak for login
    Auth-->>U: 4. User enters credentials, submits
    Note left of Auth: Keycloak authenticates user.
    Auth-->>U: 5. Redirect back to KAINAM with<br/> temporary Authorization Code
    U->>KAINAM: 6. Browser sends Auth Code to KAINAM's<br/> backend callback (/callback?code=...)
    KAINAM->>Auth: 7. KAINAM backend exchanges Auth Code<br/> for JWT Access/Refresh Tokens (server-to-server)
    Auth-->>KAINAM: 8. Keycloak returns JWTs
    Note left of KAINAM: Backend creates a session and<br/>stores tokens securely.
    KAINAM-->>U: 9. Return authenticated app state